// Package win32 is the platform for classic Windows programs over user32,
// gdi32 and comctl32: a `ui.window` is a top-level window, a `ui.button` a
// BUTTON control, a `ui.input` an EDIT.
//
// Win32 is a C API, so the platform names C and no language. Its widgets are
// built by protocol functions over its runtime, C shipped beside its SNGL
// (`rt/`), and over `sngl:platform/win32/api`, the Win32 declarations
// generated from Microsoft's metadata. Win32 lays out nothing, so the runtime
// keeps a record beside each window and lays a box's children out itself.
//
// A program on win32 builds with any language that calls C. Off Windows it
// is cross-compiled with MinGW for the platform's `arch`, and `sngl run` runs
// it under Wine.
